WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.514
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:07.980
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:15.228
Unit seven: Career Paths. In this unit, you will talk about jobs, ambitions and imaginary situations.

4
00:00:16.217 --> 00:00:17.253
career path.

5
00:00:17.953 --> 00:00:21.601
career path means the series of jobs you have during your working life.

6
00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.272
Nita is still choosing her career path.

7
00:00:24.972 --> 00:00:27.671
Your turn. Say: career path.

8
00:00:30.371 --> 00:00:31.604
career path.

9
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:33.989
job satisfaction.

10
00:00:34.689 --> 00:00:37.919
job satisfaction means the feeling of enjoying your job.

11
00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:40.405
Doctors often have high job satisfaction.

12
00:00:41.105 --> 00:00:43.513
Your turn. Say: job satisfaction.

13
00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:47.760
job satisfaction.

14
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.798
career change.

15
00:00:50.498 --> 00:00:53.763
career change means moving to a completely different type of work.

16
00:00:54.063 --> 00:00:57.223
At forty, my uncle made a career change from banking to teaching.

17
00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:00.564
Your turn. Say: career change.

18
00:01:03.264 --> 00:01:04.300
career change.

19
00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:06.737
qualification level.

20
00:01:07.437 --> 00:01:11.550
qualification level means how high your education or training certificates are.

21
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.465
This job requires a high qualification level.

22
00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:18.096
Your turn. Say: qualification level.

23
00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:22.215
qualification level.

24
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:24.462
work experience.

25
00:01:25.162 --> 00:01:28.461
work experience means the time you have spent working in jobs.

26
00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:32.026
She gained work experience in a hotel during the summer.

27
00:01:32.726 --> 00:01:35.193
Your turn. Say: work experience.

28
00:01:37.893 --> 00:01:39.219
work experience.

29
00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:41.554
salary increase.

30
00:01:42.254 --> 00:01:45.357
salary increase means more money for doing the same job.

31
00:01:45.657 --> 00:01:48.028
He asked his boss for a salary increase.

32
00:01:48.728 --> 00:01:51.589
Your turn. Say: salary increase.

33
00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:55.801
salary increase.

34
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:57.725
job market.

35
00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:01.365
job market means the number and kinds of jobs available.

36
00:02:01.665 --> 00:02:04.315
The job market for IT workers is very strong.

37
00:02:05.015 --> 00:02:07.272
Your turn. Say: job market.

38
00:02:09.972 --> 00:02:11.171
job market.

39
00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:13.335
employer brand.

40
00:02:14.035 --> 00:02:18.043
employer brand means the reputation a company has as a place to work.

41
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:20.587
Google has a famous employer brand.

42
00:02:21.287 --> 00:02:23.974
Your turn. Say: employer brand.

43
00:02:26.674 --> 00:02:28.105
employer brand.

44
00:02:29.117 --> 00:02:31.000
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.776
Nita, if you could choose any job, what would you do?

46
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:38.186
If I had the chance, I would become a software engineer.

47
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:41.425
Why does that career path interest you?

48
00:02:42.717 --> 00:02:46.295
The job market is strong, and I would have high job satisfaction.

49
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:50.210
If you needed work experience, where would you look?

50
00:02:51.517 --> 00:02:55.490
I'd apply for an internship at a company with a good employer brand.

51
00:02:56.783 --> 00:02:58.969
Grammar focus: Second conditional.

52
00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:03.288
Use the second conditional for imaginary or unlikely situations.

53
00:03:03.588 --> 00:03:06.157
If plus past simple, then would plus verb.

54
00:03:06.457 --> 00:03:10.209
For example: If I had more time, I would learn Japanese.

55
00:03:10.509 --> 00:03:12.904
We often say 'If I were you' to give advice.

56
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:16.894
Now read and listen. Choosing a Career in Cambodia.

57
00:03:17.194 --> 00:03:20.854
Cambodia's job market is changing quickly as the economy grows.

58
00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.891
Today, there is high demand for workers with digital and language skills.

59
00:03:27.183 --> 00:03:31.238
Many graduates would choose a different career path if they could start again.

60
00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.115
Experts say that work experience is often as valuable as a high qualification level.

61
00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:42.622
Internships are a great way to find out what really gives you job satisfaction.

62
00:03:43.917 --> 00:03:46.395
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:46.695 --> 00:03:49.600
Moving to a completely different type of work is a blank.

64
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:54.923
A, salary increase. B, career change. C, job market.

65
00:03:58.917 --> 00:04:01.392
The answer is B: career change.

66
00:04:02.883 --> 00:04:06.090
If I blank rich, I would buy a house for my parents.

67
00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.730
A, am. B, were. C, will be.

68
00:04:13.717 --> 00:04:15.171
The answer is B: were.

69
00:04:16.683 --> 00:04:19.623
If she studied harder, she blank the exam.

70
00:04:19.923 --> 00:04:23.658
A, would pass. B, will pass. C, passes.

71
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.580
The answer is A: would pass.

72
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:34.209
The reputation of a company as a workplace is its blank.

73
00:04:34.509 --> 00:04:38.569
A, employer brand. B, career path. C, work experience.

74
00:04:42.583 --> 00:04:44.850
The answer is A: employer brand.

75
00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.476
According to the text, which skills are in high demand?

76
00:04:49.776 --> 00:04:54.892
A, digital and language skills. B, farming skills. C, driving skills.

77
00:04:58.883 --> 00:05:01.696
The answer is A: digital and language skills.

78
00:05:03.183 --> 00:05:07.287
Now it's your turn to speak. If you could have any job in the world, what would it be?

79
00:05:12.587 --> 00:05:18.987
If I could have any job, I would be a travel journalist, because I love writing and exploring.

80
00:05:19.287 --> 00:05:20.833
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:25.512
Great work today! You learned eight new words and second conditional.

82
00:05:25.812 --> 00:05:29.138
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

83
00:05:29.438 --> 00:05:31.614
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

84
00:05:31.914 --> 00:05:34.892
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

